# The production stack's `.env` — a template, never the real file.
#
# The real one is /home/archi/stacks/filesdrop/.env on the host that runs the
# stack, mode 600, and it is never committed or stored as a Woodpecker secret
# (issue #1, Decision 13). deploy/refresh.sh copies this template there on the
# first deploy and then refuses to start the stack until TUNNEL_TOKEN and
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD are filled; the rest are optional (see each one).
# See deploy/README.md.

# The `filesdrop` tunnel's token, from Cloudflare Zero Trust → Networks →
# Tunnels → filesdrop → Configure (the value after `--token` in the install
# command). It is the credential for the whole tunnel.
TUNNEL_TOKEN=

# The database password. It is put into DATABASE_URL unescaped, so keep it
# URL-safe: `openssl rand -hex 32`. refresh.sh generates one when this is empty
# on the first run. Changing it later does not change the password of an
# existing database volume — that needs ALTER USER inside postgres first.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=

# ─── password-locked files (issue #20) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Signs the short-lived access tokens that unlock a password-protected file.
# `openssl rand -hex 32`. Changing it only logs out people who had unlocked a
# file in the last few minutes.
FILE_ACCESS_SECRET=

# ─── Telegram bot (issue #20) — optional ───────────────────────────────────────
# The bot and its local Bot API server (compose profile `bot`) start only when
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN, TELEGRAM_API_ID, TELEGRAM_API_HASH and BOT_API_KEY are
# ALL set. Leave any of them empty and the site deploys without the bot.

# From @BotFather (/newbot, or /token for an existing bot). The bot's whole
# identity: whoever has it can act as the bot.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=

# The local Bot API server's credentials, from https://my.telegram.org →
# API development tools (create an app once; any name). api_id is a number,
# api_hash 32 hex characters. They identify the app, not the bot.
TELEGRAM_API_ID=
TELEGRAM_API_HASH=

# Shared between the bot and the api: an upload carrying it is rate-limited per
# Telegram user instead of per IP. `openssl rand -hex 32`.
BOT_API_KEY=
